 [17592186421886 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534448 17592186045417 true] [17592186421886 1071 "Suppose $(4a+2b)\\cdot a=0$, where $a\\ne 0.$ Which of the following statements are true? \n\nI. $a\\cdot a<0$\n\nII. $b\\cdot a=\\frac{1}{2}$\n\nIII. $b\\cdot a=-2(a\\cdot a)$" 13194139534448 17592186045417 true] [17592186421886 1072 #uuid "34e8f50c-adbf-51d4-b0d4-a2150385ab67" 13194139534448 17592186045417 true] [17592186421886 1074 "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false. Since $a\\ne 0,$ we must have $a\\cdot a>0.$\n\n- Statement II is false since it leads to a contradiction. If $b\\cdot a=\\frac{1}{2}$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4a+2b)\\cdot a & =0 \\\\ 4(a\\cdot a)+2(b\\cdot a) & =0 \\\\ 4(a\\cdot a)+2(\\frac{1}{2}) & =0 \\\\ a\\cdot a & =-\\frac{1}{4},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nbut this is a contradiction since $a\\ne 0$ implies that $a\\cdot a>0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. Simplifying the expression $(4a+2b)\\cdot a=0$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(4a+2b)\\cdot a & =0 \\\\ (4a)\\cdot a+(2b)\\cdot a & =0 \\\\ 4(a\\cdot a)+2(b\\cdot a) & =0 \\\\ 2(b\\cdot a) & =-4(a\\cdot a) \\\\ b\\cdot a & =-2(a\\cdot a)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that the correct answer is \"III only\"." 13194139534448 17592186045417 true] [17592186421887 1068 #edb/ref 17592186421885 13194139534448 17592186045417 true] [17592186421887 1069 "q-74045" 13194139534448 17592186045417 true] [17592186421887 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139534448 17592186045417 true] [17592186421887 1071 "Suppose ${b}_{2}=q{b}_{1}+a$ and ${b}_{1}\\cdot {b}_{2}=-4.$ If $a=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ and ${b}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]$, find the value of $q.$ \n\n*Hint: You might wish to take the equation ${b}_{2}=q{b}_{1}+a$ and find the dot product of both sides with ${b}_{1}.$*" 13194139534448 17592186045417 true] [17592186421887 1072 #uuid "5008b167-e8a9-508a-9bad-146a4857fbba" 13194139534448 17592186045417 true] [17592186421887 1074 "First, we take the equation ${b}_{2}=q{b}_{1}+a$ and find the dot product of both sides with ${b}_{1}$, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{2} & =q{b}_{1}+a \\\\ {b}_{1}\\cdot {b}_{2} & ={b}_{1}\\cdot (q{b}_{1}+a) \\\\ {b}_{1}\\cdot {b}_{2} & ={b}_{1}\\cdot (q{b}_{1})+({b}_{1}\\cdot a) \\\\ {b}_{1}\\cdot {b}_{2} & =q({b}_{1}\\cdot {b}_{1})+({b}_{1}\\cdot a)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the formula for the dot product to compute the values of ${b}_{1}\\cdot {b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{1}\\cdot a:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1}\\cdot {b}_{1} & ={b}_{1}^{2}+{b}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & ={3}^{2}+{4}^{2} \\\\  & =9+16 \\\\  & =25 \\\\ {b}_{1}\\cdot a & ={b}_{1}{a}_{1}+{b}_{2}{a}_{2} \\\\  & =3\\cdot 1+4\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =3+8 \\\\  & =11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the values for ${b}_{1}\\cdot {b}_{1},$ ${b}_{1}\\cdot a,$ and ${b}_{1}\\cdot {b}_{2},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{b}_{1}\\cdot {b}_{2} & =q({b}_{1}\\cdot {b}_{1})+({b}_{1}\\cdot a) \\\\ -4 & =q\\cdot 25+11 \\\\ -25q & =15 \\\\ q & =-\\frac{3}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534448 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-09065806-b133-53e7-a415-f60daab53b99" 17592186421874 "answer-0ff61a3d-11e1-5c24-a4c0-eb5c2f727280" 17592186421875 "answer-105fb53f-a973-5605-818d-1c2b476234cd" 17592186421876 "answer-201f2230-7957-57ee-9f4c-64a64340bee2" 17592186421877 "answer-650f79ed-8cca-54b7-b878-11eaac10aaa0" 17592186421878 "answer-71b3b29c-1c8b-59df-b6b7-57376201da06" 17592186421879 "answer-7545ce1c-fbdd-52ac-ac9c-cfeceb2c4411" 17592186421880 "answer-8aef25aa-ccf6-5e00-8e61-47a0af94462a" 17592186421881 "answer-aad07bb7-3639-5c8d-96b9-7f614d3b5f47" 17592186421882 "answer-fa68821a-605f-5327-b1d5-cc2363ae0488" 17592186421883 "answer-field-612fca8f-e7e8-5291-ad03-38fa3749ba41" 17592186421884 "answer-field-cb20dfa1-3b66-5467-a387-ca9ce4c4fd61" 17592186421885 "question-34e8f50c-adbf-51d4-b0d4-a2150385ab67" 17592186421886 "question-5008b167-e8a9-508a-9bad-146a4857fbba" 17592186421887} :edb/committed false :e